# Managed by Ansible (remote-devbox). Overrides Ubuntu's vendor tmp.conf, whose
# 10-day retention can exhaust the tmpfs inode budget under agent build workloads.
# tmpfiles only removes entries whose access, modification and change timestamps
# are all older than this age, so active work remains protected.
q /tmp 1777 root root 3d

# /tmp is a tmpfs sized at half of RAM, so everything written there is resident memory
# that cannot be reclaimed — only swapped. That is fine for locks and sockets, and ruinous
# for the multi-gigabyte scratch trees container tooling produces: one SBOM scan left
# 10 GiB of unpacked image layers here, and with a bun install tree beside it the box sat
# at 87% memory stall with the CPU idle, killing the memory daemon repeatedly. Retention
# does not help — the damage is done in minutes and the policy above measures days.
#
# So give agents a TMPDIR on disk instead. The unit files and profile launchers point
# TMPDIR at this developer's directory; Codex treats $TMPDIR as its own sandbox writable
# root, distinct from /tmp, so a sandboxed command can still write here.
d /var/tmp/devbox-scratch 0755 root root -
{% for dev in devbox_developers %}
q /var/tmp/devbox-scratch/{{ dev.user }} 0700 {{ dev.user }} {{ dev.user }} 3d
{% endfor %}
